  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response Nutrition Gaza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the escalating health and nutrition crisis in Gaza, the IRC, will implement a targeted emergency nutrition intervention, aimed at stabilizing the nutrition situation, preventing excess morbidity and mortality, and strengthening community resilience in Deir al-Balah and Khan Younis. The primary goal is to reduce acute malnutrition and promote healthy feeding practices among children under five and Pregnant and Lactating Women (PLWs), while strengthening community-based nutrition systems. The prolonged conflict, large-scale displacement, and collapse of essential services have severely affected food security, infant feeding, and access to health and nutrition care. The project will apply an integrated delivery model combining Community-based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM), Infant and Young Child Feeding in Emergencies (IYCF-E), and micronutrient support. Activities will include community screening and referral, provision of Ready-to-Use Therapeutic Food (RUTF) and essential nutrition commodities, counselling on optimal breastfeeding and complementary feeding, and promotion of hygiene and maternal care practices.</narrative>
  </description>
